# Registered exemptions from the host-toolchain policy.
#
# docs/design/build.md section 0 is the policy; tests/host-toolchain-lint.sh is
# what enforces it; this is the list of invocations that break it today and the
# reason each one is still here. An exemption is allowed. An UNEXAMINED path is
# not, and neither is a waiver that outlives what it waived: the lint fails when
# a rule here matches nothing, so a renamed file or a fixed call site turns this
# file red rather than leaving a rule behind about something that is gone.
#
# Format: path<TAB>tool<TAB>reason. One row per (file, tool) pair, not per line.
#
# THE REGISTER IS EMPTY, and that is a state worth recording rather than a file
# nobody got round to deleting. It held six rows when PLAN-080 section 5.5
# opened it. RFCT-318 took three off by moving gen-dev-keys.sh and the two
# judges into pinned containers. PLAN-080 backlog B7 took the last three --
# the two hack/check.sh scripts and the workflow that ran them -- by making
# .github/workflows/check.yml reach the Rust gate through tests/rust-gate.sh
# instead of a rustup toolchain it installed. Those scripts now declare
# themselves container-side at the top of each file, which they could not
# honestly do while one of their two callers was a bare host.
#
# Keep the file. The lint reads it when it is here and treats its absence as
# empty, so deleting it would change nothing today and would remove the format
# documented above on the day somebody needs a row.
